    "narrative": "Our offensive output today hinges on **Corbin Carroll**, who sits as our elite anchor with a 78.75 score. While he faces Nick Lodolo, whose 4.68 xERA suggests a prime opportunity to drive scoring, **Corbin Carroll** overcomes the negative platoon impact through pure speed and volume in the #2 hole, providing the highest ceiling for our scarcest category, SB. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.49) and **Isaac Paredes** (65.97) follow closely as top-tier plays. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Troy Melton, with his dynamic platoon edge acting as the primary catalyst for his high efficiency rating, while **Isaac Paredes** continues to be a locked-in start thanks to his favorable park conditions and a strong command of the #3 spot.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer today was bypassing **Cole Young** (47.73) in favor of the current starting configuration. While **Cole Young** maintains high sprint speed\u2014an asset we prize\u2014his projected placement in the bottom third of the lineup limited his total efficiency score compared to the aggressive, top-of-the-order usage of **Henry Bolte** and **Mickey Moniak**. **Mickey Moniak** (59.91) in particular remains a high-variance play; he enjoys a massive 14% park boost, though his score is slightly tempered by a poor platoon split against the southpaw Joey Cantillo. **Travis Bazzana** also secures a spot, largely driven by a massive 14% park advantage and an 8% boost from hitting second.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that every single slot is currently \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have built our projections on historical expectations, managers should keep a close watch on confirmation; any shifts into lower-order slots could quickly crater the efficiency of fringe starts like **Jose Caballero** or **Zach McKinstry**. Furthermore, while **Austin Riley** (41.96) remains on the bench, he serves as our primary pivot should any last-minute defensive replacements or injury scratches force a shift in our strategy against his tough matchup with Jacob Misiorowski.",
